  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Between the Modules",
      "items": [
        "Green arrows are Integration Events and Snapshots, written to the Outbox in the publishing Unit of Work's commit and delivered to each subscription; no Module references another Module.",
        "Inventory and Billing reference Catalog's Contracts and never Catalog: Inventory receives ProductCreatedV1, ProductCreatedV2 and ProductSnapshotV1, Billing ProductCreatedV1 under its own subscription.",
        "Ledger, a Stream Module, publishes AccountOpenedV1 in the commit that activates the account; Billing receives it through Ledger's Contracts and opens a welcome quote.",
        "Billing schedules ExpireQuote as a delayed command; Inventory declares ReconcileStock as a recurring command for the system Actor inventory.stock-reconciler."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The two Hosts",
      "items": [
        "With ConnectionStrings:broker, ModularMonolith.Host composes Catalog, Billing and Ledger under the service name modular-monolith, and Inventory.Host composes Inventory under the service name inventory; what Catalog publishes then reaches Inventory over RabbitMQ.",
        "Inventory.Host composes ModularMonolith.ServiceDefaults; ModularMonolith.Host does not.",
        "ModularMonolith.ReverseProxy composes the service defaults and PouryaKit.ReverseProxy, runs no Operation, and routes every path to ModularMonolith.Host, whose liveness probe its settings turn off; under the AppHost it routes Inventory's paths to Inventory.Host, with the probe on.",
        "ModularMonolith.ServiceDefaults references EF Core Relational for its readiness check, OpenTelemetry, service discovery, Serilog, PouryaKit.Web and PouryaKit.Observability.",
        "ModularMonolith.AppHost, an Aspire AppHost, runs both Hosts and the Reverse proxy as processes on PouryaKit.Aspire's containers, giving each the connection strings its composition reads: with the broker, ModularMonolith.Host leaves Inventory to Inventory.Host. Run with LocalAgent=true, it adds Ollama and points that Host's agent at it.",
        "ModularMonolith.Host also composes PouryaKit.Reporting.Module, a Kit package no template packs, with its one report kind, SalesReports, and stores the reports in an S3 bucket."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The templates",
      "items": [
        "PouryaKit.Templates keeps no copy of the business code: it packs the sample Modules' code, the service defaults recipes and three files of ModularMonolith.Host when the package is packed.",
        "Each template's Host, project files and smoke test are the template's own; the monolith takes Catalog without Modularity, and Ledger, a second write model, stays in the modular monolith; the service takes Inventory and Catalog's Contracts alone, with Inventory.Host's composition and no Reverse proxy."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
